  "question": {
    "text": "A block of mass $M$ is pulled along a horizontal frictionless surface by a rope of mass $\\mathrm{m}$. If a force $\\mathrm{P}$ is applied at the free end of the rope, the force exerted by the rope on the block is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "0WEJE",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{Pm}}{\\mathrm{M}+\\mathrm{m}}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "WoGDz",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{Pm}}{\\mathrm{M}-\\mathrm{m}}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "T6Odp",
      "text": "\n$P$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "C1b73",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{PM}}{\\mathrm{M}+\\mathrm{m}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Since the displacement for both block and rope is same so, the acceleration must be same for both\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/7EriFigkOEAuJP-b6bkAWXuLK3VCK_ebKjnF0uGY3Yo.original.fullsize.png\"><br><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/a2IrsKMGEx-TUKk3aB3Dt3TAB93AxBmrOCSaHKHXHWc.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n$\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{p}=(\\mathrm{m}+\\mathrm{M}) \\mathrm{a} \\quad \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{a}=\\frac{\\mathrm{P}}{\\mathrm{m}+\\mathrm{M}}$\n$\\mathrm{T}=\\mathrm{M} \\cdot \\mathrm{a}=\\frac{\\mathrm{PM}}{\\mathrm{m}+\\mathrm{M}}$",
    "image": null
  },
